    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d581-a1">

                <pb facs="0548" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg478"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arosemena</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzalez</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">D. D. No. 1785</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-10-23">October 23, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I am pleased to refer to Your
                    Excellency’s favor No. 271 of the 22nd instant.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d581-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>My Government has received with special approbation the information which Your
                    Excellency gives us in relation to the dispositions contained in the last laws
                    issued by the United States Congress and approved by the Executive Power, on the
                    work of laying out and constructing the proposed Inter-American Highway, and
                    accepts with pleasure the determined route across Panama in the report of the
                    survey which Your Excellency kindly sent to us on the 11th of June of this year
                    as an enclosure to your Note No. 191.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>J. D. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Arosemena</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
